xMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7718100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq","html_url":"https://github.com/neikeq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T00:34:25Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T00:34:25Z","body":"It seems that `GetNestedType(\"GodotInternal\")` returns a generic type definition, even though it's called on a constructed generic.\n\nOne way to solve this would be to use `MakeGenericType`. But that's not AOT-compatible, and I think we are probably using AOT on some platforms, right?\n\nAlternatively, as a temporary workaround, we can generate a helper method like this:\n\n```cs\npartial class GenericNode<T> {\n    static Type GetGodotClassGodotInternalType() {\n        // Resolves to a constructed generic type within this context.\n        return typeof(GodotInternal);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nOnce #118932 is merged, we can get rid of that workaround, as that PR doesn't rely on reflection for this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5881354452/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]